<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tekyeh Dowlat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1868</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Takyeh Dowlat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tekyeh Dowlat was a royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> built in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a> by Naser al-Din Shah in 1868 near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golestan-palace">Golestan Palace</a> for performances of the ta'zieh, the passion plays that commemorate the martyrdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">Imam</a> Husayn at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-karbala">Karbala</a>. A large circular building seating thousands of spectators, it was the grandest venue of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> religious theatre. It was demolished in the 1940s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tekyeh-dowlat.jpg" alt="Tekyeh Dowlat" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HanSilo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Courtyard_in_Golestan_Palace.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
